A||||5||PatrickB||Bad Fuel Pump?||||8||
Z||000000||PatrickB||01-17-2001||07:44 PM||||I was just trying to work on something before I bring it to the shop to get fixed because I dont have the time.  Heres the deal.<P>My fiero died on me one morning when I was trying to start it.  I tried to start it but it wouldnt start.  I checked it the next day and I am getting good spark to all the cylinders.  I checked the relays and they are good.  If I floor the gas pedal I can get it to start but it idles poorly and will stall when I take my foot off.  <P>I was thinking that the fuel pump was mostly likely shot but I dont have a guage to test the pressure.  When I turn the key I can hear the pump pressurize and stop and I can smell gas when Im cranking it so I am thinking that the pressure is no good.<P>Im trying to get some more opinions before I bring it over.  Its an '86 GT.<P>Pat||||reg||8
Z||000001||88formula||01-17-2001||08:10 PM||||Your engine is getting flooded because you can smell gas and it starts when you put it into clear flood mode (flooring the gas pedal). If you can hear the fuel pump and it sounds normal than chances are it's OK. When you floor the gas pedal and then try to start the engine that puts the computer into clear flood mode. In this mode the computer will not fire the fuel injectors. If your engine runs in this mode for a long period of time than it is getting fuel some other way.<P>I cannot think of why it would be getting flooded that bad except that maybe the cold start injector is stuck on or the return line for the fuel injection is plugged. Try unplugging the cold start injector and see what happens. Also try to start the engine with a vacuum line or two unplugged to lean out the mixture. If it starts and runs better than you know for sure that the engine was flooded. <P>When it runs with the gas pedal floored is there allot of black smoke?<P>If you remove one of the spark plugs is it wet with fuel or is it dry?<P>Do you see raw gas coming out the exhaust?<P><BR>Good luck and let me know what it was.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Eric_PA||01-17-2001||08:15 PM||||The one thing that comes to my mind. Is there oil pressure? Maybe your oil pressure sensor is bad and not allowing for the fuel pump to stay on.<P>I just went back and read your post. You wrote "If I floor the gas pedal I can get it to start but it idles poorly and will stall when I take my foot off. " <BR>I had the same problem, it ended up being a bad EGR valve.<P>All I can think of,<BR>Eric<p>[This message has been edited by Eric_PA (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||PatrickB||01-17-2001||10:35 PM||||Thanks 88Formula I will try it out tomorrow.  There was some black smoke coming out of the engine when it was running but I just figured it was extra gas and junk from trying to crank it over.  Didnt see any actual gas coming from the exhaust though.   Eric, I checked the oil pressure gauge and sender and it was fine.  The pressure climbs up as I crank over the engine.  <P>I just noticed today that if I floor it, it will start but idle poorly.  If I dont put my foot on the gas it will crank over and it sounds like it almost catches but doesnt.  I was figuring that the pump was barely pumping out gas and when I floored it it was giving enough to run.<p>[This message has been edited by PatrickB (edited 01-17-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||01-18-2001||01:17 AM||||we had one here in the shop acting that way - we changed the cold start injector and put in new plugs (the others, even though they were relatively new, wouldn't fire due to being fouled continuously), changed those and it fired right up and runs like a new one! -- try the cold start injector and new plugs.||||reg||1
Z||000005||PatrickB||01-18-2001||03:14 AM||||Can someone tell me the easiest way to disconnect/disable the cold start injector?  I was looking through my Haynes and it doesnt have much info.<P>Im going to try replacing my plugs(could use it) and disabling the cold start injector and see whats happens.<P>I appreciate everyones help!<P>Pat||||reg||5
